= Practice Questions (Exam Pattern)

Ten questions designed in authentic CUET UG single-correct style. The official marking scheme awards $+5$ for each correct answer and deducts $-1$ for every incorrect answer.

#mcq(1, [On which date did the United Nations officially come into legal existence following the ratification of the Charter by the permanent members?], (
  [26 June 1945], [24 October 1945], [30 October 1945], [10 December 1948],
))

#mcq(2, [On which date did India formally sign the United Nations Charter, becoming an original founding member state of the world body?], (
  [15 August 1947], [24 October 1945], [30 October 1945], [26 January 1950],
))

#mcq(3, [Which country joined as the 193rd sovereign member state of the United Nations General Assembly in July 2011?], (
  [Montenegro], [East Timor], [South Sudan], [Switzerland],
))

#mcq(4, [The non-permanent members of the United Nations Security Council are elected by the General Assembly for a term of how many years?], (
  [1 year], [2 years], [3 years], [5 years],
))

#mcq(5, [Which principal organ of the United Nations suspended its formal operations on 1 November 1994 with the independence of Palau?], (
  [Economic and Social Council], [Trusteeship Council], [International Court of Justice], [Human Rights Council],
))

#mcq(6, [The International Court of Justice (ICJ), comprising 15 judges elected for 9-year terms, is permanently headquartered in which city?], (
  [Geneva, Switzerland], [New York, USA], [The Hague, Netherlands], [Vienna, Austria],
))

#mcq(7, [Which UN Secretary-General died tragically in a plane crash in the Congo in 1961 and was posthumously awarded the Nobel Peace Prize?], (
  [Trygve Lie], [Dag Hammarskjöld], [U Thant], [Kurt Waldheim],
))

#mcq(8, [The World Trade Organization (WTO) officially succeeded the General Agreement on Tariffs and Trade (GATT) on which date?], (
  [24 October 1945], [1 January 1991], [1 January 1995], [11 December 2001],
))

#mcq(9, [The International Atomic Energy Agency (IAEA), established under Dwight Eisenhower's 'Atoms for Peace' initiative in 1957, is headquartered in:], (
  [Geneva], [Paris], [Vienna], [London],
))

#mcq(10, [The international coalition formed by regional rivals (such as Pakistan, Italy, Argentina) to oppose the G4 bid for permanent UNSC seats is known as:], (
  [The Non-Aligned Movement], [Uniting for Consensus (Coffee Club)], [The Global South Coalition], [The Cairns Group],
))

= Detailed Solutions

#solution(1, [The United Nations officially came into existence on 24 October 1945, which is celebrated internationally as United Nations Day.], answer: [B])

#solution(2, [India signed the UN Charter on 30 October 1945 in San Francisco, becoming an original founding member state of the United Nations.], answer: [C])

#solution(3, [South Sudan was admitted as the 193rd sovereign member state of the United Nations in July 2011 following its peaceful independence referendum from Sudan.], answer: [C])

#solution(4, [Under Article 23 of the UN Charter, the 10 non-permanent members of the Security Council are elected for staggered 2-year terms and cannot be immediately re-elected.], answer: [B])

#solution(5, [The Trusteeship Council suspended its formal operations on 1 November 1994 following the independence of Palau, the last remaining trust territory.], answer: [B])

#solution(6, [The International Court of Justice (ICJ) is the only principal organ of the UN located outside New York; it is permanently seated at the Peace Palace in The Hague, Netherlands.], answer: [C])

#solution(7, [Dag Hammarskjöld of Sweden, the second UN Secretary-General, was killed in a suspicious plane crash in Northern Rhodesia (now Zambia) in September 1961 during the Congo peace mission.], answer: [B])

#solution(8, [The WTO was formally established on 1 January 1995 following the 1994 Marrakesh Agreement, taking over the mandate of the provisional GATT framework.], answer: [C])

#solution(9, [The IAEA was established in 1957 and is permanently headquartered at the Vienna International Centre in Vienna, Austria, to inspect civilian nuclear programs.], answer: [C])

#solution(10, [The 'Uniting for Consensus' group (popularly nicknamed the 'Coffee Club'), led by Italy, Pakistan, Mexico, and Argentina, opposes the expansion of permanent UNSC seats for the G4 nations.], answer: [B])

